  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australian Development Investments (ADI) Pilot Window - Technical Assistance &amp; Management Fees</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This investment is the technical assistance and fees contribution for Australian Development Investments (ADI) Pilot Window. It also includes DFAT administration costs (up to $513,000) for DFAT&apos;s administration of the program. The funding cap for ADI&apos;s Pilot Window is $40 million. The window funding is made up of Bill 1 (technical assistance and fees, $15.87 million) and Bill 2 (investment capital, $24 million). Bill 2 (investment capital) is housed under another program fund. ADI is Australia&#x2019;s $250 million impact investment fund of funds. ADI makes early-stage and concessional investment into promising impact investment funds in the lndo-Pacific. These funds then provide financing to small and medium enterprises (SMEs) across the region. ADI focuses on SMEs that deliver climate and gender equality outcomes. Further information on ADI can be found on its website: https://adi.fund/.</narrative>
  </description>
